(version 1)

# Custom DRC rules for the CNC-milled sub crossover board.
#
# Copper is isolation-milled with an 0.8 mm flat end mill, so 0.8 mm is the hard
# floor on any copper-to-copper gap: the tool cannot enter anything narrower, and
# a gap it cannot enter stays shorted. The Default netclass asks for 0.85 mm, which
# gives every routed track ~0.025 mm of copper either side of the cut as margin for
# runout and registration.
#
# Four through-hole parts have a pad pitch fixed by the component's own legs, with
# a copper gap below that 0.85 mm target:
#   * JP1, JP2 - 1x06 pin header, 2.54 mm pitch -> 0.84 mm pad-to-pad
#   * JP3      - 1x02 pin header, 2.54 mm pitch -> 0.84 mm
#   * U2       - TO-220 (pads already narrowed to 1.7 mm) -> 0.84 mm
# Those gaps are a property of the part, not of anything we cut, and 0.84 mm still
# clears the 0.8 mm tool in a single pass. The rules below relax the clearance ONLY
# between two items that both belong to that specific footprint. The full 0.85 mm
# stays in force for every gap between DIFFERENT components and for all tracks.
#
# U1 (DIP-14 LongPads) is 0.94 mm and needs no exception.

(rule "JP1_intra_pad_clearance"
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('JP1') && B.memberOfFootprint('JP1')")
	(constraint clearance (min 0.8mm)))

(rule "JP2_intra_pad_clearance"
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('JP2') && B.memberOfFootprint('JP2')")
	(constraint clearance (min 0.8mm)))

(rule "JP3_intra_pad_clearance"
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('JP3') && B.memberOfFootprint('JP3')")
	(constraint clearance (min 0.8mm)))

(rule "U2_intra_pad_clearance"
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('U2') && B.memberOfFootprint('U2')")
	(constraint clearance (min 0.8mm)))
